---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/href';

const endpoint = 'https://api.landback.land/api/mcp';
---

<Page
  title="Talk it through with an AI assistant"
  lede="Connect an AI assistant to this atlas and ask it about the land where you live: whose homeland it is, the treaties that took it, the promises broken, and who you can support."
>
  <p>
    The atlas runs a read-only <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/">Model Context Protocol</a>
    server. An assistant connected to it looks things up in this atlas instead of guessing, quotes
    its sources and links back to the records here.
  </p>
  <h2>Connect</h2>
  <p>Server address:</p>
  <pre class="sans"><code>{endpoint}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Claude</strong> (web or desktop): Settings, Connectors, Add custom connector, then
      paste the address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Claude Code</strong>:<code>claude mcp add --transport http landback {endpoint}</code>
    </li>
    <li>Other assistants: add a remote MCP server (Streamable HTTP) with the address above.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What it can do</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>
      <code>whose_land</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>The treaty history of an address, town, ZIP code or point.</dd>
    <dt>
      <code>get_record</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      One treaty, cession, nation, case or violation, with its sourced summary and connections.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>search_atlas</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>Find records by name, including other names and spellings.</dd>
    <dt>
      <code>support_the_work</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      The nations and organizations restoring land and law for a nation or state, with links to give
      on their own sites.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <h2>Ask it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>“Whose land is 1234 Pine Street, Missoula, Montana? How was it taken?”</li>
    <li>“Which treaty promises were broken where I live, and what happened in court?”</li>
    <li>“Who is working on land return near me, and how can I help?”</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    The assistant only knows what this atlas records, and the atlas is an early release: nothing has
    been reviewed by a Native nation or a lawyer yet. It cannot speak for any nation. Nothing it
    says is legal advice. Addresses go to the Census Bureau’s geocoder and are not stored; see
    <a href={href('/privacy/')}>privacy</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
